20. Fraud Model
Authoro cannot guarantee intellectual authorship.
Threats include:
* one person typing another person's work
* AI output manually retyped
* simulated typing
* compromised issuer credentials
* falsified timestamps
* unauthorized account access
* collusion
* malicious editor integrations
Authoro should therefore always describe provenance evidence precisely.
A valid proof means:
This signed evidence was recorded and has not been altered.
It does not inherently mean:
Every underlying claim is objectively true.

