Copyright is different
I would not sell “copyright clearance” the same way.
Copyright exists automatically when qualifying original expression is fixed; registration isn't required for copyright to exist. (U.S. Copyright Office)
And the Copyright Office's public records system mainly contains registration/recordation metadata; it specifically says the public record does not contain copies or reproductions of the works themselves. (U.S. Copyright Office Public Records)
So searching the copyright database cannot tell you:
“Nobody owns copyright in anything similar to this.”
Instead offer two separate things:
Copyright Record Search “Are there registrations matching this title/author/work?”
and
Originality Search “Does substantial text from this work appear elsewhere?”
The latter is really your plagiarism product.

