61. Revised North Star
The original North Star remains valid:
Authoro should not become the place everyone writes. It should become the place everyone checks.
This Addendum adds a commercial corollary:
The record should remain open. Strengthening, automating, protecting, researching, and professionally managing that record is where Authoro gets paid.
That distinction is strategically important.
The free product creates the network.
The paid products increase the quality of evidence within that network.

62. Long-Term Product Identity
Authoro should resist becoming:
* another AI detector
* another plagiarism checker
* another writing application
* another blue-check social network
* another copyright filing service
Those can all become capabilities.
The larger identity should remain:
Authoro is provenance infrastructure for creative work.
Its simplest recognizable consumer interaction becomes:
A✓
or another distinctive Authoro A-mark.
A reader sees it.
They click.
They see:
* who claims authorship
* which identities were verified
* who observed creation
* which AI systems participated
* where and when the work was published
* whether the artifact still matches
* whether outside services analyzed it
* whether any claims have been corrected, disputed, or revoked
The logo therefore carries two meanings naturally:
A = Author / Authorship / Authoro
and
✓ = evidence exists behind this claim
That is exactly the kind of compact symbol that could eventually work without requiring the full Authoro wordmark beside it.
